WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.103
-You can see my first guest
every weekday on "The View."

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:07.106
Her 2020 holiday collection
is available.

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:08.641
Now, look at this.
Look at this scarf.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.010
Can you see that?
It moves. It has things.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.712
Nordstrom.com.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:15.982
You can also see her
in Stephen King's "The Stand,"

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:20.586
which premieres December 17th
exclusively on CBS All Access.

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:23.223
Look at this. Here she is,

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.091
Whoopi Goldberg!

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.527
Whoopi!
-Whoo! Yay!

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.795
-You are the best.
I love you, buddy.

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:31.764
Always something fun.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.399
Always festive.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:37.069
You are the best. Why should
this year be any different?

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:39.539
-Well, you know,
I thought about that.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.975
I thought to myself,
"What do I do?"

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:44.176
And I knew I couldn't
do a sweater,

00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:45.611
'cause who was going out?

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:47.179
Nobody.
-Yeah.

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:48.581
-[ Chuckles ]
Nobody's going out.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.416
They're not partying
in sweaters.

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:51.551
-Nope.
-No.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.253
So let's do scarfs and masks.

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.588
-Scarves and -- And it's so warm
and it's good and --

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.789
-Yeah.

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:59.992
-We need comedians at this time
in our life.

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:03.496
-Yes. We are very important
to everything, I think.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.730
-I agree.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.800
And another tradition
that you --

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.902
See, even through Zoom,
you come through.

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.905
-It breaks my heart.
I couldn't bring you --

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:14.640
'Cause you know I always
like to bring you sweets.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.912
And all I could do
was give you one cupcake.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:21.047
-But look at it.
-One cupcake.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.548
-Look at that.
Look at that, though.

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.850
You did still deliver,

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.786
and, honestly, Whoopi,
you have to see.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.054
Dave, could we have a two shot

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.390
so Whoopi could see
where I'm at, the wide shot?

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:33.693
This is me here.
There's nobody here.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.227
-Ah.
-Hi, buddy.

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:37.429
There's no Roots.
There's nobody.

00:01:37.429 --> 00:01:38.598
But we're gonna get there.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.467
But right now,
it's just me and my cupcake.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.135
-Well, that's not bad.

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:45.037
-And I'm gonna take a bite
for good luck right now,

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:46.873
because if this is from Whoopi,

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:50.476
it's always good luck
and good vibes.

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:52.277
Mmm!

00:01:52.277 --> 00:01:54.447
-It's incredibly sweet,
isn't it?

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.515
I can see your teeth
are rolling up.

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:59.586
[ Laughing, stammering ]

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:00.886
Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:03.255
That's what happens when
I give it to my granddaughter,

00:02:03.255 --> 00:02:07.093
my great-granddaughter.
She's like, "Ooh, sugar!"

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.528
-Yeah. That's like a Red Bull
right there.

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:10.730
-It's absolutely true.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.766
-That is delicious. Magnolia.
-Yes.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:18.104
-But I like your background,
what you have back there.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:21.040
Are you into the Baby Yoda,
it looks like?

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.674
-I am. I love --

00:02:22.674 --> 00:02:24.077
You know, I love him.

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.277
-I do, too.
-Because he's looking --

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:26.946
He wants to go home.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.916
But the thing
that I love, like, a lot

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.517
is that I have a relationship.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:32.719
Watch. Oh.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:35.822
[ Toy coos ]

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.023
-Are you joking?

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.391
-You rub his head like this.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.060
-Oh, no!
[ Toy coos ]

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.761
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:42.761 --> 00:02:44.363
He is --
[ Toy whooshing ]

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:45.831
Are you joking me?

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:47.466
I love it!

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:48.568
-Is that the greatest?

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.269
-How great is that show,
by the way?

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.071
Jon Favreau just crushing it.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.306
-You know, he does an
extraordinary job,

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:56.141
and it's just great.

00:02:56.141 --> 00:02:59.712
And you want to be part of it,
and you want to watch.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:03.449
And, you know, it's fun,
and, you know, you need it.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.717
And you need a Baby Yoda
in your life.

00:03:05.717 --> 00:03:06.953
-You know what I saw?

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.022
There's a documentary
on The Comedy Store

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.757
that I was flipping
through the channels,

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:14.327
and you were on it, and
I could not stop watching it.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.962
I watched the whole --
-And Mike Binder did it.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.331
-Mike Binder, and I was like --
At first, I go,

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.366
"Who is he? I know him.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.301
But I forget
where I know him from.

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.671
His voice is familiar."
Then I go, "Oh, Mike Binder.

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:26.139
I totally know Mike Binder."

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.408
He directed "Indian Summer,"

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:29.909
which is one of
my favorite movies.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:33.012
But talk to me
about The Comedy Store.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.380
What do you remember about it?

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.516
Because it's a comedy club
in Los Angeles,

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:40.619
and there's three rooms, is it?

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:42.121
Or two on the floor?

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.922
-There was two...

00:03:43.922 --> 00:03:46.124
-And then, one upstairs.
-...and then, one upstairs

00:03:46.124 --> 00:03:48.228
which was The Belly Room.

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.529
-That's The Belly Room.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:51.864
And I got really lucky.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.466
Only female comics --

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:56.068
That's where Mitzi
put all the females.

00:03:56.068 --> 00:04:00.539
And then she -- When my show
really sort of took off,

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:02.675
she just gave me The Belly Room

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:05.278
to perform in
for as long as I wanted.

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.447
And that's what I did
and had the greatest time.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.549
And, you know,
all the great comics,

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:11.317
like, all the great comics.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.519
-Like Rodney.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.688
-Rodney Dangerfield.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:21.394
And watching Richard Pryor do
what he did from the wheelchair.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:24.830
He was in the wheelchair
and still slaying people.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:29.735
He would say stuff, and you
think, "You are saying this,

00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:33.372
and your life has shifted,
and here you are,

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:37.810
and you are still,
you know, bar none,

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:38.844
one of the greats."

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:43.316
And, also, Robin
I saw there quite a bit.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:46.051
And it's a wonderful --

00:04:46.051 --> 00:04:49.188
It's a wonderful memory,

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.323
'cause you just --
You don't think about it

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:53.326
while you're doing it.
-While you're doing it.

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:58.698
-You only realize how amazing
it was when you get past it

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.232
and you're doing your own thing.

00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:02.835
And they were all like,
"What do you do?"

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.937
I was like, "Well,
I kind of tell stories."

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:07.173
And they were like, "Really?"
I was like, "Yeah."

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.141
They said, "Okay,
let's go and see."

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:11.911
So, you know,
'cause people would say,

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.346
"Well, you're not a stand-up."

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:16.181
And I was like, "No, I'm not,
'cause I can't tell jokes."

00:05:16.181 --> 00:05:20.153
I can mess up a joke
better than anybody.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.088
You know, I just --
I'm not good at them.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:23.923
But I'm a good storyteller.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:26.959
-But is that where Mike Nichols
came to see you?

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:30.730
-No, Mike came to see me
downtown in Manhattan.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:34.000
It was great,
'cause he was taking --

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.403
He was doing all three plays
at the same time,

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:43.443
"Hurleyburley," "Death of a
Salesman," and "The Real Thing."

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.476
-Whoa.

00:05:44.476 --> 00:05:47.746
-So he decided --

00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:50.683
They would take each other
to different shows,

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:53.386
and that was the show
that he got taken to.

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:57.990
And it was quite amazing
to see him,

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:02.761
because he would say, you know,
"Ms. Goldberg, how are you?"

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:04.663
And I'd be, "I'm fine.

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:05.964
I'm fine."
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:05.964 --> 00:06:08.401
And my mother was like,
"That's Mike Nichols."

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:10.869
-Yeah. Gosh.
-They would point and look

00:06:10.869 --> 00:06:12.405
and, you know.
-Genius.

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:19.211
-It's still to me as ridiculous
and fabulous as it was day one.

00:06:19.211 --> 00:06:23.482
The whole ride is ridiculous
and fabulous to me.

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:25.551
-Yeah, I agree.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:28.020
And you're acting again,
which is great.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.855
You're in Stephen King's
"The Stand."

00:06:29.855 --> 00:06:31.223
I want to talk to you
about this.

00:06:31.223 --> 00:06:32.724
I know that you would be
totally into it,

00:06:32.724 --> 00:06:35.060
and you're like, "Oh, this is
perfect. I want to be in this."

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:37.095
So let's talk about Stephen King
when we come back, alright?

00:06:37.095 --> 00:06:39.598
More with Whoopi Goldberg
when we come back, everybody.

00:06:39.598 --> 00:06:42.901
-[ Rapping indistinctly ]

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:45.071
♪ Yeah, on top
of the boss meter ♪

